# Committed symlinks that are DELIBERATE — the allowlist for
# scripts/committed-symlink-check.sh.
#
# This file is empty, and that is the intended steady state. A committed symlink
# is self-referential on exactly one machine and dangling on every other: PR
# #2907 committed api/deps -> /opt/barkpark/api/deps, which stops `mix` running
# on any checkout that is not the prod box.
#
# Before adding a line here, prefer: commit the real file or directory, or
# generate the link at build/deploy time. If a symlink genuinely IS the artifact,
# add its exact repo-relative path below with a comment saying why.
#
# An entry that stops describing a committed symlink FAILS the check — a stale
# exemption is a hole nobody is watching, so exemptions cannot rot into
# permanent ones.
#
# One repo-relative path per line. `#` starts a comment.
